  "adviceMessage": "Airbag Warning Light failure has occured.There is a problem in the airbag system or the seat belt pretensioner system.This light blinks or comes on for several seconds when the ignition switch is turned to “ON” position or the engine/power switch is pressed to change the ignition mode to ON, so you can check if the light is working.The light will come on and stay on if there is a problem in the airbag system or the seat belt pretensioner system.WARNINGIf the airbag warning light does not blink or come on briefly when the engine/power switch is pressed to change the ignition mode to ON, stays on for more than 6 seconds, or comes on while driving, the airbag system or the seat belt pretensioner system may not work properly, which could result in serious injury in the event of a crash.Have both systems inspected by a Maruti Suzuki authorized workshop.",
